From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0123: blueline display power: the power button blanks the
 panel (ios-sweet 0079 fade), optional DCS display off / sleep in

backboardd calls IOMobileFramebuffer selector 12 (RequestPowerChange,
seen in our logs: "backboardd sel 12 in 1/0") with 0 when the power button
or auto-lock turns the display off, and 1 on wake. AppleCLCD ignored it,
so the panel kept showing the last frame.

As ios-sweet 0079 (and ios-sailfish 0167): while off, the vsync timer
dims the panel memory, blacks it on the next vsync, stops copying frames;
on wake the latest frame is copied again. The Pixel 3 panel (LG SW43408)
is an AMOLED, so black is pixels off. bluefb_power=0 ignores the call.

bluefb_dcs=2 (the default since 2026-11-21; 0 turns it off, 1 only logs
the DSI0 and PINGPONG_0..3 registers ABL left, read-only) also puts the
panel into display off + sleep in once black (DCS 0x28, 0x10, as Linux
panel-lg-sw43408 unprepare) and back with 0x11, 135 ms, 0x29 (its
prepare), from the DSI0 command FIFO (downstream
dsi_ctrl_hw_cmn_kickoff_fifo_command, ios-sailfish 0168), with the MDP
autorefresh stopped around the commands (upstream
dpu_hw_pp_disable_autorefresh). A command that does not complete turns
the DCS path off for the rest of the boot.

---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 268 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 267 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

